WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:07.600
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going to&nbsp;
explain an American science fiction thriller film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:15.920
called “Awake.” Spoilers ahead!&nbsp;
Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:23.520
Jill Adams is a former U.S. Army medic and a&nbsp;
recovering alcoholic. She works as a security&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:29.840
guard in a local medical college to raise her&nbsp;
kids, Noah and Matilda. At the beginning of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:35.920
movie, she enters the hospital at night and uses&nbsp;
her privileges to sneak into the research lab.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.720
She then steals some medicines and sells them&nbsp;
to a local drug dealer the next morning. 
&nbsp;

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:46.000
After the adventurous morning, Jill goes to her&nbsp;
mother Doris’ house to pick up her children.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.520
Because of Jill’s past with drug abuse, Noah and&nbsp;
Matilda are currently under Doris’s custody by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.520 --> 00:01:02.800
law. Matilda is delighted to meet her mother but&nbsp;
Noah, like a typical teenager, seems grumpy. Doris&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.480
sees them off but asks Jill to bring the kids&nbsp;
home by seven. As they drive, the car swerves and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:13.760
stops by the side of the road. The mother asks her&nbsp;
kids if they are okay but before they can reply,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:19.040
a car hits them and sends them flying into a&nbsp;
lake. The family struggles to get out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:25.120
flooding vehicle. Jill and Noah somehow manage&nbsp;
to swim up but notice that Matilda is nowhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.480
to be seen. To their relief, a policeman has&nbsp;
saved her and has brought her to the shore. 
&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.760
Jill is hurt, so the policeman suggests she go&nbsp;
to a hospital. He reveals that the entire city is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:41.280
going through a power crisis and everything that&nbsp;
works on electricity or gas is malfunctioning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.560
All the vehicles in the city have&nbsp;
stopped working out of the blue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.600
which has caused several accidents everywhere.&nbsp;
Jill and the kids rush to the hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:55.440
only to see that it is packed because of cases of&nbsp;
accidents. No one knows what caused the power loss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:00.640
or when it is going to come back but the people at&nbsp;
the hospital speculate that they might be at war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:10.640
or are being attacked by a terrorist organization.&nbsp;
As the family waits for someone to attend to them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:15.520
they witness two patients who were in&nbsp;
a coma, waking up at the same time.
&nbsp;

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:20.800
They come back home and stay at Doris for the&nbsp;
night. Noah and Jill cannot fall asleep, so they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:25.600
look at the stars through the window and notice&nbsp;
satellites moving at high speed. The following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:30.560
morning, Jill cycles to work. Even though it is&nbsp;
still pretty dark, everyone in the neighborhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:35.840
is awake. She is confused because normally&nbsp;
the streets are empty at this time of the day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:40.880
Before going to work, she goes to her drug dealer,&nbsp;
who tells her that he can double the price on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:45.440
any pills she can provide as the sales are&nbsp;
skyrocketing because of the power loss.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:50.240
At work, Jill takes the risk and tries&nbsp;
stealing medicines in the broad daylight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:55.440
She is caught by the college’s chief Dr. Murphy&nbsp;
who walks into the room with two soldiers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.760
To Jill’s surprise, the last thing they&nbsp;
care about is her stealing the medicines.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:04.160
They are preoccupied with finding the cause&nbsp;
of the power loss. Doctor Murphy remembers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.800
that Jill used to be a medic, so she asks&nbsp;
her to join the survivors’ hub established&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:14.000
to research the power loss. Jill declines the&nbsp;
offer, wanting to be with her kids instead. 
&nbsp;

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.720
An employee from the college named Brian tells&nbsp;
Jill that no one in the city has been able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.760
fall asleep for the last forty-eight hours. They&nbsp;
are unsure what is causing it but it is almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:29.520
as if the power loss eradicated human’s ability&nbsp;
to fall asleep. Brian explains the severity of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:34.240
the situation claiming that people will soon&nbsp;
suffer from the symptoms of sleep deprivation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:42.160
and if this goes on for long enough everyone&nbsp;
will lose their minds. Jill doesn’t believe him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:47.760
because Matilda slept peacefully the entire night&nbsp;
and was fast asleep when she left for work. Brian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.720
is shocked because the only known person who has&nbsp;
slept in the past forty-eight hours is an old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:57.600
woman with heart disease. The doctors have been&nbsp;
studying her symptoms in the hopes of finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.880
a cure for the condition. Jill realizes that&nbsp;
Matilda and the woman are the only exceptions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:08.240
in the entire city. Brian asks Jill to take&nbsp;
Matilda to the hub to help the doctors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:13.680
but Jill declines, fearing the experiments that&nbsp;
the doctors will perform on her daughter.
&nbsp;

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.400
Following that, she rushes home to look for&nbsp;
Matilda but finds out that she is in the church&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:23.680
with Doris. Everyone at the church has been told&nbsp;
that Matilda can still sleep. The pastor gives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:30.080
a sermon about Matilda being a beacon of hope.&nbsp;
Now, the extremists present in the Church want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:35.760
sacrifice her in the hopes of getting their sleep&nbsp;
back. Back home, Jill senses that Matilda might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.920
in great danger if people find out she can sleep.&nbsp;
So, she packs up a bag of necessities, deciding to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:48.560
run away from society. She and Noah make their way&nbsp;
to the Church and Brian tags along. On their way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:54.000
they witness several robberies take place. They&nbsp;
also come across the dead body of a police officer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:59.520
in an alleyway. People have already started&nbsp;
going insane because of sleep deprivation. Jill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.240
finally reaches the Church and hears the people&nbsp;
discuss if they should sacrifice Matilda. 
&nbsp;

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.040
Brian tries to convince the people to let her go&nbsp;
to the hub and help the scientist develop a cure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:15.200
but a police officer who is in the favour of&nbsp;
sacrificing her shoots him dead. Everyone panics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:20.720
and starts running around. Amidst the chaos, Jill&nbsp;
manages to get her children, and the three run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:27.200
to a nearby forest. Noah convinces Jill to go to&nbsp;
the hub because if he and Jill die in a few days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:33.200
people will kill Matilda. While discussing their&nbsp;
next move, Jill realizes that some old models&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:39.840
of cars must still be working. So, they go to a&nbsp;
nearby garage to find one. Noah and Matilda hide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:45.760
outside as Jill carefully walks inside the garage.&nbsp;
She notices two thugs have looted the place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:51.920
and are planning to claim all the cars as their&nbsp;
own. Jill walks further inside and manages to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:57.600
the keys, all while staying hidden. After finding&nbsp;
a car that works, they start their journey to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:03.120
hub. A while later, Matilda sleeps on the&nbsp;
back of the car. Given the circumstances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:10.880
Noah is astounded by his sister’s ability to&nbsp;
sleep. They stop the vehicle when they see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:16.000
an accident in the middle of the streets. Jill&nbsp;
walks closer and notices the thugs from earlier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:21.440
have been killed in an accident. She simply&nbsp;
takes their gun and continues the journey. 
&nbsp;

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.920
A while later, they come across a bunch&nbsp;
of naked people, presumably from a cult,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:30.720
standing in the middle of the road. To Jill’s&nbsp;
relief, they leave space for the car to pass.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:38.560
The family then reaches a secluded&nbsp;
library and decides to take a rest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:44.080
Jill teaches Matilda to shoot a gun claiming&nbsp;
that she will need it after Jill and Noah die&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:50.240
of sleep deprivation. The thought of being alone&nbsp;
terrifies Matilda. Later, she is sleeping outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:55.840
in the car while Noah and Jill are trying to&nbsp;
locate the hub on a map. Several prisoners are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:01.520
let free from a nearby prison because of the&nbsp;
crisis. A prisoner named Dodge finds the car&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:06.800
and drives away with Matilda still inside of&nbsp;
it. When the other two come outside, they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:12.320
surprised to see that Matilda missing. To add to&nbsp;
their problems, the other prisoners surround them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:17.760
asking Noah to come over. Jill runs out of bullets&nbsp;
and the criminals are about to capture them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:23.280
when Dodge drives the car back to the library.&nbsp;
He saves Jill and Noah and drives away.
&nbsp;

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:29.520
Moments later, they stop near the plane wreckage.&nbsp;
Dodge finds several clothes and other necessities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:34.960
in the wreckage, after which they head north&nbsp;
to the hub. At night, Jill teaches Matilda to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:40.480
drive to prepare her for the possibility of living&nbsp;
alone. While they are at it, they notice people’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:46.240
dead bodies hanging upside down by the side of the&nbsp;
road. Jill hurriedly tries to drive away but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:52.080
maniacs outside break the car’s window and grab&nbsp;
them through it. As they struggle to stay inside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:57.440
Matilda presses the gas and they somehow&nbsp;
manage to drive away. Some hours later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:02.960
they finally reach the hub. Jill and the kids&nbsp;
hand the car over to Dodge so he could drive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:08.640
to his hometown to meet his family. He offers to&nbsp;
stick around to help them, but they decline. 
&nbsp;

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:13.200
Jill then keeps Noah and Matilda hidden in a&nbsp;
house, because after everything that happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:18.160
on the way, she wants to make sure the hub is&nbsp;
safe for her children. The sleep deprivation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.400
is starting to get to her. She approaches&nbsp;
the hub while hiding under a bridge. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:28.000
finds out that the army protecting the hub is&nbsp;
surviving on medicines but slowly, they are also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:33.520
turning violent. Jill disguises herself as a&nbsp;
lab worker and meets the old woman who is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:39.120
only person that can sleep other than Matilda.&nbsp;
Jill wants her to raise Matilda since only she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:45.360
has a possibility of surviving. But the woman is&nbsp;
too sick and old to understand her request.
&nbsp;

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:50.960
She reveals that she was supposed to be dead last&nbsp;
month but is somehow still living. Just then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:57.200
Dr.Murphy enters the room and sees them talking.&nbsp;
Jill claims that she is there to help. Murphy is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:02.560
also visibly affected by the lack of sleep. She&nbsp;
says that the doctors have found a drug that helps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:07.840
the sleep-deprived brain function better for a&nbsp;
short period of time, but it also harms the brain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:16.080
Jill returns to the house and sees that&nbsp;
Dodge, Noah, and Matilda have been found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:21.440
by the soldiers. Dodge had come back to help&nbsp;
them, but now all of them are at gunpoint.
&nbsp;

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:26.400
To save their life, Matilda tearfully admits&nbsp;
that she can sleep. The soldiers then take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:33.120
her to the lab. The researcher, Dr. Katz exposes&nbsp;
her to an anesthetic gas and is surprised to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:39.040
that she can actually sleep. Jill has now lost&nbsp;
her rationality because of sleep deprivation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:44.640
and exhaustion. Murphy asks her questions about&nbsp;
Matilda but she can hardly form a sentence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:50.160
Following that, the old lady goes into cardiac&nbsp;
arrest and passes away despite the doctor’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:56.400
effort to save her. Now, the fate of humanity&nbsp;
is in Matilda’s hands. Dodge is taken as a guard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:01.840
and is given stimulants to help with exhaustion.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, Jill experiences hallucinations where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:07.440
she sees Noah trying to kill her. She comes&nbsp;
back to senses when a soldier takes Noah away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:12.560
who was beside her the whole time. 
As time passes, everyone at the hub, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:18.240
the medical staff and the soldiers starts to lose&nbsp;
their minds. They experience hallucinations and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:24.320
shoot everyone around them. One of the soldiers&nbsp;
calls Jill, Sandra and tries to kill her. Moments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:30.480
later, she shoots herself dead. Then, they start&nbsp;
killing each other. Jill rushes to save Matilda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:36.800
but Murphy stops her. Some seconds later, she dies&nbsp;
because of the stimulants Dr. Katz has given her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:42.640
Jill finally frees Matilda, and they run to save&nbsp;
Noah. Noah, on the other hand, is hallucinating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:48.560
too. He touches an electric wire, believing it to&nbsp;
be a fish, and gets electrocuted in the process.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:53.360
Jill and Matilda try their best&nbsp;
to save him but to no avail.
&nbsp;

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:57.360
The following morning, dead bodies are&nbsp;
scattered all around the establishment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:03.040
Everyone has died except for Matilda and Jill.&nbsp;
Yet, Jill is not in her right senses and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:09.280
about to pass out anytime soon. Suddenly, Noah&nbsp;
wakes up alive and well. The two are surprised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:14.640
and overjoyed to have him back. They notice that&nbsp;
Noah seems to have come back from a deep sleep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:19.920
and is now normal. Matilda registers that&nbsp;
Noah could sleep because he temporarily died&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:24.640
last night like she did when she drowned in&nbsp;
the lake. In an attempt to save their mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:29.120
the kids bring her to a nearby lake. They&nbsp;
push her into the water, waiting for her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:34.640
to stop moving. When she goes limp, they bring&nbsp;
her out and try to revive her. The movie ends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:42.240
as the kids perform CPR on their mother. 
